From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf: Do not flush the nodes on a seek from pause.

The media session no longer flushes its nodes when a paused presentation is
started at a new position (added by 4010). The sources' seek already resets
the stream; flushing the transforms and sinks as well left the playback
without samples after the seek, and in the mf tests a later session's start
with a shut-down source never reported MESessionStarted: the test spun until
it was killed (mf.c:6476 on x86_64, 117 failures, deterministic - not load,
as 4010's notes thought). The flush on stop, and its dropping of queued
transform events, stay.

Gate: test/mf-seekpause-gate.sh (64/32).
---
 dlls/mf/session.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mf/session.c b/dlls/mf/session.c
index f4caa03..f7dbda2 100644
--- a/dlls/mf/session.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/session.c
@@ -1128,9 +1128,12 @@ static void session_start(struct media_session *session, const GUID *time_format
                 return;
             }
 
-            /* Starting a paused presentation at a new position is a seek: drop what is in flight. */
+            /* A seek from pause does not flush here: the sources' seek does what is
+             * needed, and flushing the nodes too left the stream without samples. */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_SEEKPAUSE_FLUSH
             if (session->state == SESSION_STATE_PAUSED && start_position->vt != VT_EMPTY)
                 session_flush_nodes(session);
+#endif
 
             LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(source, &session->presentation.sources, struct media_source, entry)
             {
